After ascending a gnomish archeologist today after a good 20 tries, I
was taking a look at the various race/role/alignment combinations to
see what it would take to win with every possible combination.
(There's a table here: http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Player) Now, I
can, perhaps, understand why Knights and Samurai must be lawful
humans, but why on Middle Earth can only humans and elves play
priests? Do gnomes, dwarves, and orcs have no religion? Sure, dwarves
hate magic so they shouldn't get to play Wizards, but why do they get
to be Valkyries? And why can't an Elf be a Healer - is it because that
role wouldn't be appropriate for a Chaotic?

For perspective, I've been playing Nethack (vanilla, strictly) since
version 3.1.0, before races existed; Elf was a class then. I'm just
trying to figure out the justification for why the roles were set up
this way.

